Just had my first ascension ever, no special conduct other than I didn't
wish for any artifacts (mainly because by the time I could, I'd already
seen 6 or so artifacts in the game and didn't think I'd get one).  I'd
only made it to Gehennom once before for real, although I did play through
in wizard mode once (died like 13 times on the way to the fake ascension).
 
Juliet Valk AC-51 HP 456 St25 Co18 De18 Int21 Wis22 Cha17
Neutral Level 30
 
Been playing Nethack for over a decade and played Rogue on the PC Jr back
in the 80's, by this point I'm extremely spoiled.
 
It was version 3.1.x, since I don't have a 'net connection at home.  AFAIK,
I didn't abuse any bugs in that version or anything.
 
Didn't find a shirt (T or Hawaiian) all game.  Didn't find any unholy
water, so wound up using 2 wishes in the Planes for cursed ?o$Detection--
is there a better way to do that?  Would a cursed ?ofRemoveCurse work?
I had one but didn't want to risk playing around with it.  Also, got
polymorphed a couple of times in the mid-game, which I think killed my
hit points (see below).

I've never really done #twoweapon since I tried it early in the game and
couldn't hit a thing.  After reading here I guess I should do that next
time, though having a shield is nice.
                                                                                
ANYWAY:
                                                                                
Juliet started off her career without any major pieces of good luck--no
real early wishes or pieces of the ascension kit.  She did find a
]oDisplacement on level 1, but it was promptly destroyed on level 2.
In retrospect, the placement of a scroll shop on level 3 and potion shops
on 4 and 5, all of them pretty large, was a big help--she managed to
price-identify a lot of stuff early on and pick up a bunch of ?ofIdentify
for later use.
                                                                                
Also found a +1 pair of dwarvish shoes and dwarvish mithril early on,
giving her a pretty decent AC.  Decided to go down the mines to Minetown,
where there was a cross-aligned altar; darn.  Bought about 8 points of
protection from the priest anyway.  Oh, yeah--there was a magic lamp,
got GDSM.  Weight was getting to be a major problem, turned around and
headed for Sokoban--hit an altar along the way and got Mjollnir.  Then
hit the jackpot while diluting some potions in a fountain--a water daemon
gave me a wish.  I was so worried about weight that I thought about the
bag of holding, but I decided Sokoban might have it and went for Gauntlets
of Power figuring they might help the weight problem and would definitely
help with Mjollnir.  At this point I started feeling like this game was
going places.
                                                                                
Sokoban turned out to have the "oReflection--probably a better find, but
I was struggling to stash all my stuff.  Went downward as far as Medusa's
island (didn't cross it, though) and found 2 good-size general stores and
a pair of water-walking boots (I'll need those later).  No bag, though.
                                                                                
There was a co-aligned temple around level 12 that became my base of
operations for the rest of the game--nice little closet in the room with
the temple that made for good storage.
                                                                                
Okay, back to finish the Mines.  Turns out the level immediately below
Minetown had a bones file from a previous Valk who had dropped her bag
of holding to jettison weight during her death struggle (meaning nothing
in it was cursed).  It was full of useful scrolls and potions, and about
now is when I got pretty confident that I could ascend if I played smart.
Turns out she had on a "ofLifeSaving, magic marker, and Speed Boots,
and had a bunch of valuable gems--she got waxed on the way back up from
Mine's End and had identified the glass and left it behind.  Cool.
                                                                                
Okay, finished Mine's End--didn't get the Wine Cellar, damn.  Back to
Medusa's island, got a shield of reflection from the statue of Perseus
and stoned the lady.  Still wasn't 14th level, so I went downward and
cleaned out the castle.  Two charges on the wand I think.  By this point
I had found a helm of brilliance in another store, so decided to wish
for a cloak of protection (giving me good boots, gloves, armor, shield,
helmet, and cloak) and saved a charge (still hadn't found a scroll of
charging, since I didn't *need* anything yet I figured I'd wait and
hope to find charging but could wish for it if it became critical).
 
The level below the Castle had a maze, Sunsword was laying around--damn.
Last thing I want was useless artifacts loaded.
 
Went to the temple, payed more protection money.  Got to naked AC -3 or
so.  Only had about 130 HP at this time (despite being a level 14 Valkyrie
with a 20 Constitution due to a +2 ring of gain con), I had been poly'd 2
times before getting GDSM and I think that killed my HP ("You feel like
a new woman" both times--would that be a possible way to kill HP?).
 
I had 3 scrolls of genocide, blessed them and wiped out 'L', 'h', and ';',
I never found another genocide but that was a good set to eliminate.
 
Went back up and finished the Quest, then went and finished off
Fort Ludios.  Spent most of the money on protection (AC -9 naked) and
spent a lot of time praying and sacrificing--got Fire Brand, Cleaver,
Demonbane (no Frost Brand, darn).  Decided Mojo was my best weapon,
ditched Cleaver and Demonbane, and carried Fire Brand as a backup.
Did some poly-piling and wound up with an extra AmuletoLifeSaving and
a RingofProtection +5(!!!)  The ring made up for the lack of a T-shirt,
and by the time I finished resting and regrouping I was down to AC -51,
with 12 +6 elven daggers, +6 Mojo and +7 Fire Brand (wasted 2 cursed
?EnchantWeapon trying to knock Mojo down a point, I guess blessed artifacts
don't go that way...)
 
Managed to polypile a ?ofCharging.  Wished for cursed genocide (only got
1) and did some nurse-dancing.  Between that and a couple !ofGainLevel
I got over 300 HP and headed for the Valley of the Dead.
 
So I'm basically invisible and everything resistant (including disintegration
and what have you), with -51 AC and reflection.  As it turns out, I don't
think I ever got more than 50 HP below my maximum from this point forward
(Orb of Fate is nice).
 
Cleared out the Valley, went and stashed things at base, and made my
final run (left the water-walking boots at base and went with ring of
levitation for weight reasons--I carried like 20 !ofHolyWater, in retrospect
that's overkill since I had plenty of chance to grab more from the stash
on the way out of the dungeon).
 
Early in Gehennom I hit a trap door that must've dropped me 2 levels,
then immediately hit another and wound up in Asmodeus' lair.  He gated in
Dispater, Juiblex, and Orcus--none of those proved tough.  Juiblex is a
total wimp, !ofParalysis on Orcus, and the others I found at the stairs
and dispatched neatly.  Found my way up and realized I'd fallen past
both Juiblex's swamp and Orcus Town, cleared them out.  Found 4 amulets,
poly'd up another Life Saving (so I was wearing one and carrying 2 more).
Worked my way down, found the vibrating square, tunneled out clear paths
between staircases, and then did Vlad's tower--easy!  Got another Life
Saving there, which was good because...
 
DEATH 1: Ate a dragon corpse.  Apparently a bad idea when wearing a ring
of free action, choked to death.  Dumb!
 
Okay, headed for Rodney's and took him out with a wand of death (I had 2,
one with 7 charges and one with 8).
 
Down to the vs and did the ritual, headed in to Moloch's sanctuary and
slowly fought my way through it.  Grabbed the Amulet of Yendor and ran
for the top--Rodney showed up once on the way, I gave him the smackdown.
                                                                                
On the plane of earth I broke down and used a wish for cursed gold
detection, Rodney showed up, killed him and sprinted for the portal.
Then did likewise on the plane of air--that one had me worried since I
have no idea how to kill an Archon, but I outran most everything except a
couple air elementals.  Finished Fire (Rodney showed up again), switched
to amulet of magical breathing on the water plane and swam for the portal.
                                                                                
Took a deep breath on the Astral Plane and started slogging through the masses.
Ran into Pestilence, /oDeathed him and then had a moment of indecision
wandering around.  He came back and I wasted a couple turns trying to /oDeath
him while he made me sick and dead--I should have just smacked him up by
hand, that would've left me plenty of time to grab a !ofFullHealing from
my bag and drink it.  I also should have prayed (does that work on the
Astral Plane?), I was very careful about keeping myself ready to pray safely.
Oh, well, second "ofLifeSaving gone.  Still had 2 more, put one on and
headed for the first altar.  Turned out to be the right one, #offered the
Amulet and ascended.
                                                                                
Killed 5 demons (Orcus, Dispater, Asmodeus, Juiblex, Yeenoghu), killed
Rodney 4 times and the usual assortment of nasties.
                                                                                
Whew.  Next to do it with an archaeologist.

What a great game.

